mcwsd provisions throwaway development workspaces for coding agents (FreeBSD
jails, Docker, Podman, Kubernetes and more) behind a small HTTP API, with
dependency caching, capacity gating and automatic pruning.

The runtime backend is chosen per daemon instance with --plugin; the plugins
shipped by this port live in %%PREFIX%%/share/mcwsd/plugins.

To run it as a service:

  1. Generate a client token:        mcwsd token
  2. Put it in /usr/local/etc/mcwsd.env as MCWSD_TOKEN=...
     and lock it down:               chown root:_wsd /usr/local/etc/mcwsd.env
                                     chmod 0640 /usr/local/etc/mcwsd.env
  3. Pick a plugin in /etc/rc.conf:  mcwsd_plugin="/usr/local/share/mcwsd/plugins/freebsd-jail.js"
  4. Enable and start:               sysrc mcwsd_enable=YES && service mcwsd start

See %%PREFIX%%/share/doc/mcwsd/FREEBSD-SETUP.md for the full jail walkthrough.
